msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_1"
msgstr ""
"There's something about dragons that captures the human imagination. Take a "
"look at the folklore of just about any region of the world, and chances are "
"you'll find a story involving some kind of big, reptilian creature that "
"breathes fire and guards untold treasures. In some cultures, they're "
"benevolent beings associated with wisdom and good fortune; in others, "
"they're malevolent lords of chaos who must be slain by a brave hero. In any "
"case, an encounter with a dragon is a fateful event, and the holder of a "
"dragon's tooth is a true champion indeed."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_11"
msgstr ""
"We humans are curious beasts. Survival alone isn't enough for us, like it is"
" for most animals. It's in our nature to crave stimulation and inspiration, "
"the chance to imagine and to dream. And what better way to do all that than "
"with a good book, a film, or, dare I say it, a video game like World of "
"Tanks? Each is a portal that carries us far from the mundane routine of "
"everyday life into a world where anything's possible, even if only for a "
"moment. That, if you ask me, is real magic."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_13"
msgstr ""
"Speaking of human nature, isn't it funny how we love problems? We're "
"naturally drawn to puzzles, enigmas, mysteries, riddles. We all fancy "
"ourselves as the brilliant maverick detective, don't we? The one who pieces "
"the clues together and cracks the case others thought unsolvable through our"
" intuition and sheer powers of deduction. That attention to small details "
"and analytical mindset will serve you well anywhere, whether you're working "
"on a cold case or not. And on the battlefield, they could just be the "
"difference between victory and defeat."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_14"
msgstr ""
"Nothing beats the thrill of Christmas morning when you're a kid, does it? "
"That feeling in your stomach when you wake up—if you managed to sleep at "
"all, that is—then the rush as you see the pile of presents under the tree, "
"waiting to be opened. They were never fancy presents, either. Video games "
"were pretty primitive then, and World of Tanks was nothing but a speck on "
"the horizon! But it didn't matter. That awkwardly wrapped tape player or "
"bike might not seem like much now. But back then, they meant the whole "
"world."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_16"
msgstr ""
"You know who my favourite superhero is? It's Father Christmas. I mean it. "
"He's got an iconic costume and some of the finest facial hair around. But "
"more importantly, he's blessed with the rarest superpower of all. No, not "
"the power to deliver billions of presents in just 24 hours, or to consume "
"heroic amounts of mince pies and cookies. The power to make people happy! "
"Christmas is a time of joy, and nobody does joy better than Santa. Every "
"December, we all have the chance to become a superhero just like him—by "
"giving, sharing, and spreading a bit of Christmas cheer. Costume not "
"mandatory!"

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_17"
msgstr ""
"There's a lot of talk about what it means to be a man these days. Some would"
" have you believe it's about having millions in the bank and a six-pack like"
" an action figure. I don't know about you, but that's not my style. For me, "
"a man is someone who takes responsibility for his actions. Someone who's "
"respectful and considerate of those around him. And someone who has the "
"courage to be vulnerable, without trying to be a tough guy all the time. "
"Because the measure of a man is in his actions, not his abs."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_20"
msgstr ""
"Feeling stuck, or bored, or lost all your mirth? Go travelling. No, really. "
"Buy a ticket somewhere you've never been before, or get in your car and "
"drive. Even if it's only for a day. Consider that my professional advice to "
"you. There's a whole world of adventure out there: new people and places, "
"new experiences, new perspectives. All waiting for you. And trust me, "
"wherever you go, you'll come back a different person. A little more worldly,"
" a little more alive. It won't solve all your problems, sure. But it's a "
"damn good place to start."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_3"
msgstr ""
"Much as it’s human nature to believe in mythical beasts like dragons, it's "
"also in our nature to seek adventure, new knowledge, and new experiences. "
"\"To strive, to seek, to find, and not to yield,\" as a certain poet once "
"had it. Okay, that might sound a bit much. But that adventure doesn't have "
"to mean jumping out of a plane, or an epic journey to the ends of the earth,"
" exhilarating as those may be. It can be anything that pushes us to grow by "
"nudging us just a little bit out of our comfort zone. Because, nice as it "
"may be there, things start to get really interesting the moment we step "
"outside it."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_5"
msgstr ""
"Fail to prepare, prepare to fail. Cliché, I know, but it's true. I'm a firm "
"believer in doing your research ahead of time, and being as ready as you can"
" for anything. That's especially true in tanking, where you quite literally "
"need to do your research if you want your vehicle to stand a chance on the "
"battlefield. But it's not just that. It's about knowing your strengths and "
"weaknesses, and understanding what you're up against, so you can react "
"accordingly. That way, whatever happens, you can say you gave it your all. "
"So make sure you're ready, and don't let anyone catch you off guard. Do your"
" research!"

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_6"
msgstr ""
"Have you ever wondered what it must be like to invent something completely "
"new? To create something never seen before in all of human history—something"
" that could fundamentally change our very way of life, forever? Volta, "
"Faraday, Edison, Tesla. The men who brought light to our world. All had a "
"singular focus on their goal, a belief in their vision, and, perhaps even "
"more importantly, a refusal to take no for an answer. We don't all have to "
"change the world, but there's something in that: if you believe in "
"something, then follow it through to the end, and don't let anyone tell you "
"it can't be done."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_8"
msgstr ""
"Look, it's a truth universally acknowledged that a man needs a few basics in"
" his life. A well-fitting suit. A tasteful tie, or perhaps even a bowtie, if"
" you're feeling bold. A couple of understated cufflinks. And a sleek watch "
"to round it all off. None of it has to be fancy, or cost an arm and a leg. "
"It's about making you look good, and giving you an air of quiet confidence "
"and measured authority. Because when you look good, you feel good. And when "
"you feel good, you're unstoppable."

msgid "newYear/challenge/stories/gift_a_9"
msgstr ""
"How often do you stop to look around you? Not just look, but really see. "
"It's quite remarkable how much you can learn by just observing your "
"surroundings. You know what they say: the devil's in the details. But it's "
"not just him; there's magic in them, too, if you look hard enough. Next time"
" you head out somewhere—be it the battlefield or elsewhere—keep your eyes "
"and your mind open, and try to take in all the little things you'd normally "
"ignore. You might just be surprised at what you discover."

